.Dd March 12, 2026
.Dt REQUEST_REGION 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm request_region
.Nd reserve an I/O port range in the global resource tree
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/resource.h
.Ft "struct resource *"
.Fn request_region "resource_size_t start" "resource_size_t n" "const char *name"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn request_region
function reserves an I/O port range in the global resource tree.
If the requested range overlaps an existing reservation, the request fails.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn request_region
function returns a pointer to the reserved resource on success or
.Dv NULL
on conflict or allocation failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr release_region 9 ,
.Xr resource 9
